package data

// Daily blog 2026-11-19: ICA year-end school holiday checkpoint advisory (20 Nov 2026 - 3 Jan 2027).
// Sources fetched 2026-11-19: ICA media release dated 16 Nov 2026 (all ICA figures), says.com
// 2026 MOE school holiday list (Johor = Group B, 5-31 Dec), mothership.sg 2025-11 (last year's
// advisory, for context only). The Star and Malay Mail copies of the 2026 advisory could not be read.
func init() {
	posts := []BlogPost{
		{
			Slug:          "year-end-school-holidays-2026-woodlands-tuas-heavy-traffic-20-nov-3-jan-jb-guide",
			Title:         "Year-End School Holidays 2026: ICA Expects Heavy Traffic at Woodlands and Tuas, 20 Nov – 3 Jan",
			Excerpt:       "Singapore's ICA says heavy traffic is expected at both land checkpoints from 20 November 2026 to 3 January 2027. What the advisory says, what Deepavali looked like, and how to plan a JB crossing. Checked 19 November 2026.",
			Date:          "2026-11-19",
			LastModified:  "2026-11-19",
			Category:      "Travel Tips",
			Author:        "Pelangi Capsule Hostel",
			ReadTime:      "4 min read",
			Tags:          []string{"causeway", "woodlands-checkpoint", "tuas-checkpoint", "school-holidays", "singapore-to-jb", "border-crossing"},
			FeaturedImage: "/images/blog/year-end-holidays-2026-checkpoints-cover.webp",
			ImageAlt:      "Card reading Year-end school holidays 2026, heavy traffic expected at Woodlands and Tuas, 20 Nov to 3 Jan, with a RM35 capsule from Pelangi Capsule Hostel",
			InLanguage:    "en",
			Content: `
<h2>The Short Version</h2>
<p>On <strong>16 November 2026</strong>, Singapore's Immigration &amp; Checkpoints Authority (ICA) said it expects <strong>heavy traffic at the Woodlands and Tuas checkpoints from Friday 20 November 2026 to Sunday 3 January 2027</strong>, the year-end school holiday period. ICA's advice is to plan ahead and, where you can, cross at off-peak times such as <strong>early mornings and late evenings</strong>. We read the ICA release on 19 November 2026.</p>

<figure class="blog-figure"><img src="/images/blog/year-end-holidays-2026-checkpoints-cover.webp" alt="Card reading Year-end school holidays 2026, heavy traffic expected at Woodlands and Tuas, 20 Nov to 3 Jan, with a RM35 capsule from Pelangi Capsule Hostel" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="630"><figcaption>ICA year-end advisory: 20 Nov 2026 – 3 Jan 2027.</figcaption></figure>

<h2>What ICA Said Happened at Deepavali</h2>
<p>ICA used the Deepavali long weekend (<strong>6 – 9 November 2026</strong>) as its benchmark: more than <strong>2 million</strong> travellers crossed at Woodlands and Tuas, traffic peaked on 6 November with more than <strong>553,000</strong> travellers clearing immigration at the land checkpoints in one day, and car travellers leaving at peak hours waited <strong>up to three hours</strong> because of tailbacks from Malaysia. ICA gave no forecast figures for the year-end period, so we cannot tell you which days will be worst.</p>

<h2>Malaysian School Holidays Overlap</h2>
<p>According to SAYS' list of the Education Ministry calendar, the Malaysian year-end school break for Group B states, which includes <strong>Johor</strong>, runs <strong>5 – 31 December 2026</strong> (Group A states start a day earlier). That overlaps with the Singapore window ICA describes, so crossings in both directions can be busy in December. This is our reading of two separate sources, not an official forecast. Last year followed the same pattern: ICA issued a similar warning on 17 November 2025 for the 2025 year-end holidays (reported by Mothership).</p>

<h2>Practical Checklist From the ICA Release</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Check the right passport and QR code.</strong> ICA says cases of travellers presenting the wrong passport or QR code rose from 46 in July to 74 in September 2026. These travellers are held for further checks and cannot leave Singapore until the correct document or code is shown.</li>
  <li><strong>Passport validity:</strong> at least six months remaining.</li>
  <li><strong>SG Arrival Card</strong> for short-term visitors entering Singapore: submit via the MyICA app within three days before arrival (the enhanced card has applied since 30 September, per ICA).</li>
  <li><strong>Driving a foreign-registered car into Singapore:</strong> you need a valid VEP. From 2 November 2026, foreign-registered vehicles with unpaid traffic, parking or emissions fines cannot apply for or renew a VEP and will be denied entry. See our <a href="/blog/singapore-vep-unpaid-fines-blocked-from-2-november-2026-driving-from-jb">VEP unpaid-fines guide</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Queue cutting:</strong> ICA says offenders are sent to U-turn and rejoin at the back. During the Deepavali weekend at Woodlands, 6 vehicles were directed to re-queue and 5 drivers of foreign-registered vehicles were banned from entering Singapore.</li>
  <li><strong>Live traffic:</strong> ICA points to LTA's OneMotoring site, the EMAS signs on the BKE and AYE, and ICA's Facebook and X accounts.</li>
  <li><strong>Construction:</strong> ICA notes ongoing works at Woodlands Checkpoint and at Tuas Checkpoint's departure car zone.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Our Practical Take</h2>
<p>If you are staying in JB, you control your timing. Crossing early in the morning or late at night is what ICA recommends. The advisory does not say which days are busiest, so check live traffic the day you travel. For other ways to cross, see our <a href="/blog/singapore-to-jb-day-trip-causeway-guide">Singapore to JB day trip guide</a>.</p>

<h2>Staying in Johor Bahru</h2>
<p>A capsule at Pelangi Capsule Hostel is <strong>RM35 per night</strong>, and a new guest booking direct on our website pays <strong>RM30 for the first night</strong>. Check-in starts from <strong>2:00 PM</strong>. Payment is in MYR or SGD. <a href="/book">Book direct here</a>, see <a href="/rooms">our rooms</a>, or <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>

<h2>Sources (checked 19 November 2026)</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="https://www.ica.gov.sg/about-ica/news-and-publications/media-room/heavy-traffic-expected-at-land-checkpoints-during-year-end-school-holidays--travellers-reminded-to-check-their-passports-and-qr-codes" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ICA media release, 16 November 2026</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://says.com/my/news/heres-all-the-2026-school-holidays-as-announced-by-moe" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SAYS — 2026 school holidays as announced by the Education Ministry</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://mothership.sg/2025/11/heavy-traffic-checkpoints-holidays/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mothership — 2025 year-end advisory (for context)</a></li>
</ul>
<p><small>Press copies of the 2026 advisory on The Star and Malay Mail could not be opened by us, so every ICA figure above comes from the ICA release itself. Details can change; check ICA before you travel.</small></p>
`,
		},
	}

	for i := range posts {
		posts[i].ReadingTimeMinutes = _blogComputeReadingTime(posts[i].Content)
	}
	BlogPosts = append(BlogPosts, posts...)
}
